  "question": {
    "text": "The height of liquid column raised in a capillary tube of certain radius when dipped in liquid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> vertically is, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. If the tube is dipped in a similar manner in another liquid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of surface tension and density double the values of liquid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>, the height of liquid column raised in liquid B would be ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
